<p class="lh"><strong>FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; October 30, 2024</p>

<p class="lh"><strong>Global Infrastructure Announcement:</strong> SanguineIT has opened a new regional delivery center to support rising demand for dedicated engineering squads, managed technology operations, and accelerated digital modernization programs for clients across North America, Europe, and emerging APAC markets. The new facility strengthens SanguineIT’s global delivery network and expands capacity for high-availability development and support services.</p>

<h2>Purpose behind the expansion</h2>
<p class="lh">Enterprise clients increasingly require delivery models that combine technical depth, reliable time-zone overlap, and resilient operational coverage. As transformation programs move from pilot phases into large-scale rollout, capacity constraints can delay roadmaps and increase release risk. The new delivery center was established to address these constraints with structured talent expansion, secure collaboration infrastructure, and stronger continuity controls.</p>

<p class="lh">This expansion aligns with SanguineIT’s long-term strategy to provide outcome-focused, globally coordinated delivery rather than isolated project execution. The center is designed to support both net-new engagements and scaled growth across existing client programs where velocity, governance, and support responsiveness are business critical.</p>

<h2>Capabilities introduced by the new center</h2>
<p class="lh">The facility extends SanguineIT’s operational ability across engineering, platform support, and cross-functional collaboration. Client programs can now scale more quickly while maintaining governance consistency across regions.</p>

<ul class="news-article-list">
    <li>Additional capacity for full-stack, mobile, CMS, and cloud-native engineering teams.</li>
    <li>Follow-the-sun managed operations for critical production environments and incident response.</li>
    <li>Secure workshop and sprint collaboration spaces for architecture discovery and planning.</li>
    <li>Enhanced business continuity controls including network redundancy and operational failover readiness.</li>
    <li>Faster onboarding pathways for dedicated hiring and long-term team extension models.</li>
</ul>

<p class="lh">The center also supports expanded enablement for DevOps, QA automation, and SRE practices, helping client teams move from ad hoc release execution to repeatable lifecycle governance. This improves quality predictability while reducing pressure on internal client teams managing high-demand digital backlogs.</p>

<h2>What this means for clients</h2>
<p class="lh">For global organizations, delivery location strategy has direct impact on cost efficiency, communication cadence, and operational resilience. The new regional center improves collaboration overlap with stakeholder teams, accelerates issue resolution cycles, and reinforces service continuity for programs requiring 24x7 attention. It also supports more flexible engagement options for enterprises balancing strategic initiatives with ongoing platform maintenance.</p>

<p class="lh">SanguineIT expects the center to play a central role in future growth across mobile app development, custom web platforms, cloud modernization, and product engineering engagements. By increasing execution bandwidth without sacrificing governance maturity, the company aims to help clients deliver transformation outcomes with greater confidence and speed.</p>

<p class="lh">The investment also reflects growing demand for delivery models that combine nearshore responsiveness with globally coordinated execution. As organizations scale digital programs across business units and geographies, reliable collaboration windows and standardized operating practices become critical to maintaining roadmap momentum and service quality.</p>

<p class="lh">This expansion positions SanguineIT to onboard new programs faster while preserving delivery quality expectations.</p>

